message: "If you use this dataset, code, or paper, please cite as follows."
title: "Decadal mapping of agave cultivation across the three core mezcal-producing districts of Oaxaca (Tlacolula, Yautepec, Miahuatlán; 2017–2025) using AlphaEarth Foundations embeddings — v11 production release"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Ortiz
    given-names: Iván
    email: iortiz1891@gmail.com
date-released: 2026-05-26
version: "11.0.0"
license: MIT
license-url: https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/iortiz1891/agave-boom-oaxaca-v11"
url: "https://github.com/iortiz1891/agave-boom-oaxaca-v11"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible decadal (2017–2025) record of Agave cultivation across
  the three core mezcal-producing INEGI districts of Oaxaca, México
  (Tlacolula, Yautepec, Miahuatlán; 69 municipios; ~11,850 km²), at
  10-meter resolution. The v11 classifier stacks Google's AlphaEarth
  Foundations annual embeddings (64-dim) with five terrain descriptors
  (elevation, slope, northness, eastness, TRI from Copernicus DEM GLO-30)
  and a histogram-gradient-boosting classifier
  (class_weight='balanced') trained on 4,849 photo-interpreted reference
  labels. Decision threshold tau=0.60 selected as the global F1 optimum.
  Held-out performance: overall accuracy 0.9425, Cohen's kappa 0.8018,
  agave-class precision 0.853, recall 0.821, F1 0.837 on 870 test labels.
  Raw mapped extent grows from 4,289 ha (2017) to 18,694 ha (2025),
  a 4.4-fold (+336%) increase, with the largest single-year expansion in
  2024 (+107%).
keywords:
  - agave
  - mezcal
  - Oaxaca
  - remote sensing
  - land-use change
  - AlphaEarth Foundations
  - histogram gradient boosting
  - 10-meter mapping
  - Google Earth Engine
